Notebook[
 {Cell["Lepton-quark scattering, step 2 (FORM route): spin and colour \
algebra", "Title"], Cell["Same task and same output format as the FeynCalc \
route, now with FORM doing the Dirac algebra.  Input: the amplitude records \
of step 1.  Output: Results/FORM/Algebra.wl.\n\nMathematica only writes the \
amplitudes to a file (amplitudes.inc, in the vocabulary described in \
form/common.h), runs the four FORM programs in the form/ directory, and reads \
their output back.  Open those programs to follow the algebra: Born.frm, \
Real.frm and Photon.frm square the amplitudes (conjugation, spin sums, \
density matrices, gamma traces, polarization and colour sums, kinematics), \
Virtual.frm projects the vertex graph onto the Born current.  Each program is \
run twice, with the preprocessor variable SPIN = U (spin average) and SPIN = \
P (helicity difference).", "Text"], Cell["Load and export", "Section"], 
  Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"..\", \"..\", \"FeynFacet\", \
\"FeynFacet.wl\"}]]", "Input"], Cell["records = \
LoadAmplitudes[][\"Records\"];\nwork = \
ResultsDirectory[\"FORM\"];\nWriteFORMAmplitudes[<|\"Born1\" -> \
records[\"Born\"][[1]], \"Real1\" -> records[\"Real\"][[1]], \"Real2\" -> \
records[\"Real\"][[2]],\n  \"Vertex1\" -> records[\"VirtualVertex\"][[1]], \
\"Photon1\" -> records[\"Photon\"][[1]], \"Photon2\" -> \
records[\"Photon\"][[2]]|>, work]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Import[FileNameJoin[{work, \"amplitudes.inc\"}], \"Text\"]", 
   "Input"], Cell["Run the FORM programs", "Section"], 
  Cell["program[name_] := FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"form\", \
name}];\nDo[RunFORM[program[name], work, \"Define\" -> {\"SPIN=\" <> spin}], \
{name, {\"Born.frm\", \"Real.frm\", \"Photon.frm\"}}, {spin, {\"U\", \
\"P\"}}];\nRunFORM[program[\"Virtual.frm\"], work, \"Define\" -> \
{\"SPIN=U\"}];\nFileNames[\"*.m\", work]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Born.frm (SPIN=P) prints G5Check, the difference between the trace \
Tr[gamma^a gamma^b gamma^c gamma^d gamma5] computed with the explicit gamma5 \
and -4 i eps^{abcd}; it must vanish.", "Text"], 
  Cell["bornLog = Import[FileNameJoin[{work, \"Born-SPIN=P.log\"}], \
\"Text\"];\ng5Check = StringDelete[First[StringCases[bornLog, \"G5Check =\" \
~~ Shortest[x__] ~~ \";\" :> x]], Whitespace | \"(\" | \
\")\"];\nRequire[g5Check === \"0\", \"gamma5 normalization check failed in \
Born.frm\", g5Check];\n\"G5Check = \" <> g5Check", "Input"], 
  Cell["Read the results", "Section"], Cell["FORM writes its results in \
Mathematica syntax.  Born and real squares are read as functions of D \
(through the symbol D of the declarations), the photon squares get the photon \
average 1/(D-2) and the Mandelstam names sh, th, uh; the virtual projection \
is the ratio of the numerator trace and the Born-current trace, in the family \
VirtualIntegral[n0,n1,n2], times the colour factor CF.", "Text"], 
  Cell["born = <|\"Unpolarized\" -> ReadFORM[work, \"BornU.m\"], \
\"Polarized\" -> ReadFORM[work, \"BornP.m\"]|>", "Input"], 
  Cell["Require[Simplify[(born[\"Unpolarized\"] - 2 ee^4 eq^2 ((s^2 + \
u^2)/t^2 - (4 - D)/2)) /. u -> -s - t] === 0, \"Born square differs from the \
textbook result\"];\nRequire[Simplify[(born[\"Polarized\"] - 2 ee^4 eq^2 (s^2 \
- u^2)/t^2) /. u -> -s - t] === 0, \"Polarized Born square differs from the \
expected result\"];\nreal = <|\"Unpolarized\" -> ReadFORM[work, \"RealU.m\"], \
\"Polarized\" -> ReadFORM[work, \"RealP.m\"]|>;\nFactor[real[\"Polarized\"] \
/. spe3 -> 0]", "Input"], Cell["photon = <|\"Unpolarized\" -> ReadFORM[work, \
\"PhotonU.m\"]/(D - 2), \"Polarized\" -> ReadFORM[work, \"PhotonP.m\"]|>", 
   "Input"], Cell["{numerator, bornCurrent} = ReadFORM[work, \
\"Virtual.m\"];\nvirtualFamily = Factor[numerator/bornCurrent]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Save", "Section"], Cell["algebra = <|\"Born\" -> born, \"Real\" -> \
real, \"Photon\" -> photon, \"VirtualFamily\" -> \
virtualFamily|>;\nSaveResult[\"Algebra\", algebra, \"FORM\"];\nKeys[algebra]"\
, "Input"]}, WindowSize -> {1000, 800}]
